"""latinime-dump: the keyboard layouts and geometry of AOSP LatinIME (LineageOS) as the JSON the VibeOS keyboard draws.

  latinime-dump PHONE_TREE TABLET_TREE OUTDIR
        PHONE_TREE is the LatinIME checkout the phone layouts come from, TABLET_TREE the one for the tablet's (the
        tablet's keyboard is a release newer). Writes OUTDIR/<locale>.json for every language, OUTDIR/pads.json (the
        number and phone pads) and OUTDIR/geometry.json (the sizes, per form factor).
  latinime-dump --text TREE FORM LOCALE SET ELEMENT [CONDITION=VALUE ...]
        one keyboard as text, a row per line: (label width% [background] hint= more={...}). CONDITION is one of
        the layouts' switch cases: mode=email, languageSwitchKeyEnabled=true, ...
  latinime-dump --check OUTDIR LISTING
        reads every "# kbd_... form=F locale=L set=S element=E" block of LISTING (rows in the --text notation) and
        compares it with the same keyboard as OUTDIR's JSON has it; prints the differences, exits 1 if any.

A tree is LatinIME's own repository (java/res, java/src). FORM is phone, phone-land, tablet or tablet-land: the
resource directories each would use. Python 3 standard library only.

The JSON, per language file:
  {"locale", "name" (the language's own name, for the space bar), "fullName", "set", "rows": [row, ...],
   "forms": {form: {page: [row index, ...]}}}
A page is "alphabet", "alphabet-shifted", "alphabet-locked", "symbols" or "symbols-shifted", optionally followed by
"/email" or "/url" (the field's purpose) and "+lang" (the language key shown). A row is a list of keys:
  x, w      left edge and width, in % of the keyboard's width less its side paddings
  l         label; i: icon name instead
  c         what the key does when it is not text: shift, capslock, delete, enter, space, symbols (to symbols and
            back), language, emoji, settings, clipboard_paste, shortcut, tab, next, previous, shift_enter
  t         the text it types, when that is not its label
  b         background: normal (default), functional, action, spacebar, stickyOff, stickyOn, empty
  h         hint label (top right)
  m         long-press keys: [{l|i, c, t}]; mc: their columns; mf: flags (fixed, auto, labels, dividers, noPanel)
  f         label flags, a: action flags, alt: the code typed instead while typing fast
  spacer    a gap with no key
  vl, vr    how much narrower the key is drawn than it is, on its left and right (same unit as x, w): the key
            still takes touches over its whole width
"""
